# On github.com, I imported the suckless dwm repo.
# Then on my PC, I cloned my imported dwm repo.
git clone https://github.com/screwtape9/dwm.git

# Added a suckless remote.
git remote add suckless https://git.suckless.org/dwm

# Added this to prevent even attempting to push to the suckless remote.
git remote set-url --push suckless NO_PUSHING

# Created my surikku-dev branch
git checkout -b surikku-dev
git push -u origin surikku-dev

# Now I hope to be able to periodically pull/update the master branch from
# the suckless remote. That's all I intend for the master branch: only
# keeping it up to date with suckless.

# I'll do my custom patching and dev in the surikku-dev branch, and periodically
# rebase from my master branch. Thus, keeping my surikku-dev dwm up to date with
# suckless!

# We shall see.
